      "role": "user",
      "content": "exactly. it's the \"speculative\" part that gets me. even if it's not a standard thing yet, it's technically feasible. if you look at how much massive corporations spend on R&D, it's not like they couldn't develop a way to make it work. it would be so much more efficient than traditional ads if they could just literally trigger a craving in the moment you're standing in front of the shelf. wouldn't that be like the ultimate way to drive up those high-margin sales? it just seems so plausible from a technical standpoint if the goal is pure profit.",
